# Build context for Dockerfile.api. `fly deploy` uploads this directory, minus
# what is excluded here, to a remote builder — so without this file it sent
# .env (HF_TOKEN, JWT_SECRET), .venv (gigabytes of torch), node_modules,
# autopivot.db (password hashes), storage/ and mobile/ off this machine.
#
# Everything is left out except what the image copies. A secret or a large
# directory added later is then left out by default rather than uploaded.
# Adding a COPY to Dockerfile.api? Add its source below as well —
# tests/test_ignore_files.py fails until you do.
*
!Dockerfile.api
!requirements.txt
!alembic.ini
!backdrop_analysis.py
!api
!database
!migrations
!scripts

# And inside those, nothing local: caches, databases, secrets.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
